SimTalk Access to 3D Functions
SimTalk Access to 3D Functions
Plant Simulation provides general SimTalk functions plus a number of specific functions for accessing the
3D objects.
Note
SimTalk normally does not distinguish between upper- and lower-casing for the names of methods,
attributes and read-only attributes, which you type into the source code of your Method [object].
You can view and access the attributes and methods of the 3D objects by clicking Auto Complete on the
Edit ribbon tab of the Method Editor.
Note
To access the attributes and methods of the 3D objects, type in _3D, followed by a period like so _3D.
in you instructions.
Most of the 3D attributes and 3D methods listed in the table of contents use the array data types for
setting and getting values.
See also
3D Properties Visualizing the Simulation
